  <h1>Nitro Coffee Kegs</h1>
  <p>Bona Fide packs nitro coffee in a PET coffee keg: a single-use PET keg with a Sankey D fitting, designed as a modern alternative to the stainless steel keg.</p>

  <h2>PET keg and Sankey D</h2>
  <p>The PET keg uses the Sankey D coupler found on standard draft systems, so it works with the same taps and dispensers as a traditional stainless steel keg. Because the PET keg is single-use, there is no keg to collect, return or wash.</p>

  <h2>Safety, tamper resistance and sanitation</h2>
  <p>A sealed single-use PET keg is tamper-resistant and arrives sanitary. Nothing has to be cleaned or refilled between uses, which removes a common source of contamination with reusable stainless steel kegs.</p>

  <h2>Craft Draft hot step</h2>
  <p>Craft Draft kegs go through a hot step (pasteurization) as part of the process, which supports a preserved, long-hold keg.</p>

  <h2>Efficiency and less waste</h2>
  <p>A ready-to-tap keg saves labor: there is no brewing or batching on site. A keg that holds for a long time means less coffee is thrown away, and single-use PET removes the handling and return logistics of stainless steel.</p>

  <p>See how kegs are served with <a href="/kegerators/">kegerators and dispensers</a>, read why <a href="/coffee-on-tap-is-the-future/">coffee on tap is the future</a>, or compare <a href="/cold-brew-coffee-concentrate-bag-in-box-versus-cold-brew-in-kegs/">Bag in Box versus kegs</a>. Questions? <a href="/contact-bona-fide-nitro-coffee-and-tea/">Contact us</a>.</p>
